# Demon Wall: "As long as this creature has a counter on it" means a counter of any kind, and it is judged as attackers are
# declared (CR 508.1a, 609.4). Bot1's Wall has been under its control since turn 1 and has no counter. On turn 3, in the
# beginning of combat step, Bot1 casts Requiting Hex at Bot2's Ornithopter, blighting 1 onto the Wall (a -1/-1 counter on a
# creature it controls). The Hex destroys the Ornithopter and Bot1 gains 2 life; the Wall, now a 2/2 with a -1/-1 counter,
# attacks as though it didn't have defender and deals Bot2 2. Without a counter it could not have attacked (the refusal in
# demon-wall-cant-attack-without-a-counter-and-attacks-keeping-defender-once-it-has-its-own).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Demon Wall
Requiting Hex
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Demon Wall.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Requiting Hex.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Blight 1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Demon Wall)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Demon Wall.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Demon Wall > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Demon Wall.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Demon Wall.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Demon Wall.Tapped = true
